An electron in an X-ray tube accelerates from 1.5 keV to 90 keV. If the wavelength corresponding to the minimum energy is 1.5 × 10^(-13) m and the wavelength corresponding to the maximum energy is 1.2 × 10^(-9) m, what is the frequency of the X-ray photon?
Known data:

Initial kinetic energy of electron: {eq}K_1 = 1.5\times{10^{3}} \text{ eV}=2.4\times{10^{-17}}\;     \rm{J}

{/eq}
Final kinetic energy of electron: {eq}K_2 = 90\times{10^{3}} \text{ eV }= 1.4\times{10^{-14}}\;     \rm{J}

{/eq}
Wavelength corresponding to minimum energy: {eq}\lambda_{min} =  1.5\times{10^{-13}}\;     \rm{m}

{/eq}
Wavelength corresponding to maximum energy: {eq}\lambda_{max} = 1.2\times{10^{-9}}\;     \rm{m}

{/eq}
Speed of light: {eq}c = 3  \times{10^{8}} \; \rm{m/s}

{/eq}
Planck's constant: {eq}h = 6.63\times{10^{-34}} \; \rm{m^2 kg/s}

{/eq}
Rest mass: {eq}m_0 = 9.1\times{10^{-31}} \; \rm{kg}

{/eq}
The minimum frequency received by the electron is given by:

{eq}f_{min} = \dfrac{c}{\lambda_{min}} = 200\times{10^{14}} \rm{Hz}

{/eq}

The maximum frequency received by the electron is given by:

{eq}f_{max} = \dfrac{c}{\lambda_{max}} = 2.5\times{10^{10}} \; \rm{Hz}

{/eq}

According to the Stokes-Lorenz expression for the energy {eq}K

{/eq}, this is valid:
{eq}K = h\bigg(f-\frac{1}{2}f_0\bigg)

{/eq}

Where

{eq}f = \frac{h}{K}-\frac{K}{2m_0c^2}

{/eq}

At the lower energy value, we obtain the following expression:

{eq}f_{min} = \frac{h}{K_1}-\frac{K_1}{2m_0c^2}\Rightarrow 200\times{10^{14}} \rm{Hz}= \frac{6.63\times{10^{-34}} \; \rm{m^2 kg/s}}{2.4\times{10^{-17}}\;     \rm{J}}-\frac{(2.4\times{10^{-17}})\;     \rm{J}}{2(9.1\times{10^{-31}} \; \rm{kg})(3  \times{10^{8}} \; \rm{m/s})^2}\Rightarrow 200\times{10^{14}} \rm{Hz}+2.1\times{10^{17}}\;     \rm{Hz}= 2.1\times{10^{17}}\;     \rm{Hz} + 2.4\times{10^{-17}}\;     \rm{J}

{/eq}

Then, the frequency is computed as follows:

{eq}f_{min} = \frac{c}{\lambda_{min}} = 200\times{10^{14}} \rm{Hz}

{/eq}

{eq}f_{max} = \frac{c}{\lambda_{max}} = 2.5\times{10^{10}} \; \rm{Hz}

{/eq}
####
The frequency of the X-ray photon is 200 × 10^14 Hz.

